    "result_text": "Done. There's only one test class in the project (`AcceptanceTest`), and it passes along with the full build.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe change adds a derived `timezone` field to owners, mapped from the locality/region via the fixed table (NSW\u2192Australia/Sydney, VIC\u2192Australia/Melbourne, QLD\u2192Australia/Brisbane).\n\nThree edits, each keeping structural impact low:\n\n1. **`mapper/TimeZones.java`** (new) \u2014 a small, self-contained helper with a single `zoneOf(region)` lookup and its own fixed table, mirroring the existing `Localities`/`ContactPreferences` pattern. New cohesive unit, near-zero surrounding complexity.\n\n2. **`mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 one added `@Mapping` line delegating to `TimeZones.zoneOf(...)`, reusing the exact same region derivation the adjacent `locality` mapping already uses (`customerCode.split(\"-\")[0]`). No method body grew.\n\n3. **`resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added the `timezone` schema property (read-only string) so the generated `OwnerDto` exposes the field.\n\nBehaviour lives in a new tiny class rather than expanding any existing method or class, and the mapper edit is a single declarative line.",
